listed. But **B: g4-e6** is listed — very strong.\n\nBe6 puts pressure on f1 — the king’s square. If I later play ...Qd7 and ...Rad8, White is uncomfortable.\n\nBut again, **winning a pawn is concrete**.\n\nAlso, **P: a7-a5** or **b7-b5** aim to challenge c5, but slower.\n\nBest move: **P: d4-e3** — wins a pawn, opens the d-file, and accelerates development.\n\nReason: It gains material immediately, opens lines for my rooks, and increases pressure on White’s center. Even if recaptured, I’ve improved my position and can follow up with development.\n\nAnswer: P: d4-e3'}
