ng knights or bishops (e.g., N: b8-d7 or B: g4-e6) are decent long-term plans but ignore the immediacy of promotion.\n- Castling via king-side rook movement (R: h8-g8) prepares for castling but does nothing to capitalize on the decisive opportunity.\n- The pawn promotion delivers an immediate material gain and likely decides the game.\n\nReason: Promoting the pawn on e2 to a queen maximizes material advantage with no risk. A queen is the most powerful piece and will dominate the board, especially in an open midgame. There is no tactical reason to underpromote. All other moves waste a decisive opportunity.\n\nAnswer: P: e2-e1-q'}
