r.\n\nTherefore, the best move is to block the pawn with the knight.\n\nReason: The White pawn on g6 is one move away from promotion to g7 and then queening. By playing N: f5-g7, Black occupies g7, preventing the pawn from advancing. This neutralizes a critical threat and places the knight on a strong central square near the enemy position. Other moves fail to stop the pawn effectively.\n\nAnswer: N: f5-g7"}
