: h7-h6 – prepares a later h5 push without committing en passant risk.\n  - P: h7-h5 – pushes two squares, activates the pawn toward promotion, but risks en passant capture if White had a pawn on g5 (but they don’t). Currently, no White pawn exists, so en passant isn't a threat.\n\nHowever, note that White has no pawns—only the king. So pushing my pawn aggressively is safe and desirable to promote.\n\nThe key plan is to advance the h-pawn to promote it into a queen or other piece, while using the knight and king to support this goal. Pushing the pawn immediately with h7-h5 gains tempi and gets closer to promotion.\n\nReason: The fastest way to win is to promote the h-pawn. Starting with P: h7-h5 advances it two squares toward queening with no risk (White cannot capture en passant since no opposing pawn is on g5). This also avoids wasting time. The knight and king can follow up to protect the pawn. Other moves delay this progress unnecessarily.\n\nAnswer: P: h7-h5"}
