een cannot go beyond f3.\n\nHence, **Q: h1-f3** is the furthest diagonal move possible.\n\nNow, can we deliver check? The White King is on a7.\n\nCan the queen attack a7?\n\n- From h1, queen can go to a1 (same rank) — a7 is same file as a1? No — a7 is file a, rank 7.\n\nQueen on h1:\n- Can go to a1 (rank 1) → then from a1 she controls the a-file.\n- From a1, she threatens a7 vertically.\n\nSo **Q: h1-a1** puts the queen on the a-file, one square away from a7.\n\nThen next move, **Qa1-a7+** would be check (if not blocked).\n\nBut currently, no piece blocks a-file between a1 and a7? Let\'s see:\n\nFiles:\n- a1: after queen moves to a1, it\'s occupied by Black Queen.\n- a2 to a6: all empty.\n- a7: White King.\n\nSo yes — **after Qh1-a1, next move Qa1-a7 is check, and since a8 is the only escape, and if not defended, it could be checkmate.**\n\nBut can White escape to a8?\n\na8 is currently empty. So if White King is on a7, and Black Queen checks from a1 → a7, then White King can go to a8.\n\nBut then Black can play Qa7-a8# — mate.\n\nBut only if the king cannot leave a8.\n\nBut after Ka7-a8, Qa7-a8 is capture and mate.\n\nSo sequence:\n1. ... Qh1-a1\n2. White plays something (say Kb8, or stays)\n3. ... Qa1-a7+\n4. Kxa8 → Qa7-a8#\n   Or Kc8? Wait — a7 to b8 is possible.\n\nWait — King on a7:\n- Can go to a8, b8, b7.\n\nSo after Qa1-a7+, King escapes to b8 or b7.\n\nThen no immediate mate.\n\nBut still, **Qh1-a1** exerts pressure.\n\nBetter idea: can we attack the king **now**?\n\nIs the White King on a7 under direct attack?\n\nNo Black piece attacks a7 right now:\n- Queen: not on same rank/file/diagonal unless via a1 or diagonal (blocked).\n- Knight on e4: too far.\n- King on g6: too far.\n\nSo no check yet.\n\nBut look: **Q: h1-h7** is a valid move.\n\nh7 is on the 7th rank, file h.\n\nWhite King is on a7 — same rank!\n\nSo if Black Queen moves to h7, she will be on **h7**, controlling the entire 7th rank.\n\nThus, **Qh7 attacks a7 directly** — because both are on rank