ing material or leading to faster capture.\n\nMoreover, after N: f6-d7, if White plays K: b8-a8, then I can play K: b6-b7, cutting off escape.\n\nOr if White plays K: b8-b7, then K: b6-c6 or K: b6-a6, continuing pressure.\n\nSo delivering check now improves my winning chances significantly.\n\nOther knight moves do not create immediate threats.\n\nKing moves are slow and don’t lead to quick win.\n\nTherefore, **N: f6-d7** is the best move—it delivers check and accelerates the endgame.\n\nReason: It is the only move among the options that delivers check to the White king, increasing pressure and limiting White’s options, while advancing my knight to a dominant position. This maximizes winning chances by forcing errors or leading directly to checkmate.\n\nAnswer: N: f6-d7"}
