ht lands on b7, which is adjacent to a8 — so that would attack the White king.\n\nCurrently, White’s king is on a8 — a corner square. If we move the knight to b7, it attacks a8 and c8. That delivers **check** to the White king.\n\nThat is a strong tactical move — delivering check limits White’s responses and may lead to quick progress toward checkmate, especially in a king+minor piece vs. lone king endgame.\n\nOther moves do not deliver check. For example:\n- N: c5-e6 or N: c5-d7 are slow.\n- King moves waste time when a forcing check is available.\n\nTherefore, **N: c5-b7** is the best move — it attacks the enemy king immediately.\n\nReason: Delivering check with the knight maximizes pressure, restricts White’s king movement, and makes progress toward mating net or winning the game efficiently. It uses the knight actively and exploits the poor position of the White king in the corner.\n\nAnswer: N: c5-b7"}
